# Build context is uploaded to ACR on every `az acr build`. The Dockerfile only
# needs requirements.prod.txt, core/ and products/, so exclude everything heavy.
#
# ============================================================================
# DO NOT PUT A TRAILING SLASH ON A DIRECTORY RULE. It silently does nothing.
# ============================================================================
#
# `az acr build` does not use Docker's .dockerignore parser. It builds the
# context tarball itself, in azure/cli/command_modules/acr/_archive_utils.py,
# and its IgnoreRule class strips a trailing slash ONLY inside the `if
# rule.startswith('!')` branch — so negations like `!keep/` are normalised but
# plain exclusions are not. `temp/` therefore compiles to the regex `^temp/$`
# and is matched against the tar entry name `temp`, which never matches:
#
#     temp/          -> ^temp/$          vs "temp"  -> NO MATCH  (rule is dead)
#     temp           -> ^temp$           vs "temp"  -> match     (works)
#
# Every directory rule in this file carried a trailing slash until 2026-08-24,
# so none of them had ever taken effect. The context tarball was 2.8 GB (temp
# 2.3 GB + test_uploads 494 MB) and took ~17 min to upload per product, ten
# times longer than the 1m41s build. Only .venv escaped, and not because of
# this file — the CLI hardcodes {'.venv'} in its own build_ignore_dirs list.
#
# Verify a change with tests/scripts/test_dockerignore.py, which drives the
# real IgnoreRule class rather than assuming Docker semantics.

# Virtualenv / caches
.venv
__pycache__
*.pyc
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache

# Local processing artifacts and test data
temp
files
3C_testdaten_pdf
3C_testdaten_jpg
3C_testdaten_json
3C_testdaten_md
old
benchmarks
notebooks

# Local corpora and experiment scratch. None of it is COPYd by the Dockerfile.
# test_uploads is the big one: 494 MB of real customer PDFs pulled on
# 2026-07-29 for the artifact-retention work.
test_uploads
garagenhub_input
GOT
places_experiment
handover_pruefung
bps_sanierer_input
Original_Testdaten
extraction_suite
viz_pages
converted_images
test_images
test_docs
images
results
outputs

# Repo metadata / docs / dev-only
.git
.github
docs
tests
scripts
infra
*.md
.env
.env.example
.DS_Store

# Loose media and data at the repo root. core/ and products/ hold only .py,
# .pyc and three .json schemas, so these cannot mask anything the image needs.
# Do NOT add *.json here — products/*/extract_schema.json is required.
*.pdf
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.png
*.avif
*.webp
*.csv
*.log
*.tmp
*.bak

# Dev-only requirements (prod uses requirements.prod.txt)
requirements.txt
